bdivine-dimming-fieldmouse, congenial-cibophobic-goosefish, tan-goldenrod-drever, and seaisland-nonliteral-tigermoth. Started async MCP reviews for strange-urological-cornsnake, base-conscious-astarte, priceless-hotheaded-annelid, and capable-moist-coot. Worktree fast-forwarded cleanly to origin/main@10533b1e3f651a60e8cea5691318c108ff1f3396; later remote advances reported by auditors affect unrelated paths. No code work or claims have begun.","timestamp":1788620304546019922},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Second deterministic-plan audit batch — 2026-09-05\n\nRevalidated every owned blob against `origin/main@9e6a0e436520f67962c22dc244d7b4f77f5bee45` and updated four open leaves through the repo-local CLI fallback (rebar MCP unavailable):\n\n- `nonlineal-crotchety-galago` (`51fb-a3b6-ac66-4c60`): 7 files, 10 stable docstrings; five already-concise/load-bearing ranged comments are now explicitly protected.\n- `dripping-viperous-chickadee` (`a578-8751-ec4f-4369`): 9 files, 34 stable blocks; composite ranges were split/anchored, two concise rationale blocks protected, and post-audit Terraform files excluded from this legacy inventory.\n- `twofaced-oppressed-nurseshark` (`6f06-6920-8439-4642`): 13 files, 18 stable blocks; module-size helper consumption and its focused companion test are explicit.\n- `actinium-abominable-anole` (`4458-5aec-af9b-4534`): 18 files, 43 stable blocks; the vague `and held-out narration` scope became exact IDs, six concise/load-bearing blocks are protected, and current basetemp/close-precheck/run_shape contracts replace stale audit text.\n\nAll four descriptions now require immutable before/final `type_comments=True` AST comparison with only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno` normalized, exact non-allowlisted comment/directive/runtime preservation, and one independent TSV row per edited block with immutable citations plus the three required PASS fields. Each ticket has five stru