an immutable AST/token census, exact per-file counts, deterministic base-only thresholds, and explicit protected exceptions. The current run_detectors name, timing/noqa/type-ignore/pragma directives, translated-shape/forged-attestation docstrings, and concise discovery rationale are outside the allowlist.\n\nEvery sub-8k description defines path-qualified D:/C: IDs, immutable before/final ast.parse(..., type_comments=True) comparison, removal of only allowlisted leading docstrings, ast.TypeIgnore.lineno-only normalization, rejection of changed inline/non-allowlisted comments, exact runtime/directive/shebang preservation, and one non-author TSV row per block with immutable full-SHA citations and directives_exact/semantic-preservation/bloat-removal PASS.\n\nConsumer searches covered imports, source/path guards, workflow selectors, __doc__, inspect.getdoc, and pydoc. MCP recorded exact path-specific file impact and exactly five DD commands per leaf: focused pytest with real consumers, scoped Ruff check+format, comment hygiene, owned-path diff check, and worktree-venv make verify.\n\nAll 12 leaf writes returned push_status=ok with no description or cross-session warning. Exact MCP readback matched all four descriptions, all 72 path/reason rows, and all 20 command triples. All four remain open, unassigned, and unsigned. No source edit, test/gate/plan review, claim, transition, close, code commit, or manual push occurred; these planning updates and this receipt are normal MCP ticket-event mutations auto-committed and auto-pushed by rebar.","timestamp":1788626987315194306},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Planning receipt — next four comment-remediation children\n\nImmutable audit basis: `d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84` (also the clean code-worktree HEAD and `origin/main` during preparation).\n\nSelection/ranking:\n- Rechecked the 14 eligible open, unassigned direct children and ranked the