edrock provenance, verifier, Verified-parity, identity, op-cert, wall-clock, web-tool, WIP, and workflow-name contracts.\n\nEvery description is below the 8,000-character admission cap (7,084 / 7,823 / 6,041 / 7,747 characters respectively). Each defines path-qualified `D:<qualified-owner>` and `C:<innermost-scope>:before:<unchanged-code-anchor>` IDs; immutable-before/final `ast.parse(..., type_comments=True)`; removal only of allowlisted leading docstrings; normalization only of `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; equality of all remaining ASTs; and token rejection of changed inline or non-allowlisted comments. Runtime strings, regexes, prompts, assertions, subprocess arguments, test data, shebangs, and complete directive-bearing lines are protected. Each also requires exactly one non-author TSV PASS row per block with full immutable/final citations, word counts, preserved contract/consumer, `directives_exact=PASS`, `semantic-preservation=PASS`, and `bloat-removal=PASS`.\n\nConsumer searches covered imports, source/path guards, workflow selectors, `__doc__`, `inspect.getdoc`, and pydoc. Material consumers recorded in the plans include the plan-review fixture import, dynamic redispatch loader, authorship fixture-maintenance reader, audit-server source spy, audit-page import-convention pair, API generator/docs, ADR 0059 provenance citations, wall-clock exclusion script, and verifier/web contract siblings. No runtime docstring consumer reads an allowlisted value.\n\nImmediately before mutation, MCP readback confirmed all four leaves were `open`, `assignee=null`, and `attestations={}`. Applied exactly three MCP mutations per leaf (12 total): `edit_ticket(description)`, `set_file_impact`, and `set_verify_commands`. Every result was `ok`, every `push_status.state` was `ok`, and every description/cross-session warning was null.\n\nStrict MCP readback then matched all four descriptions byte-for-byte, all 72 ordered path/reason rows exactly, and all 20 normalized DD command triples exactly. Each leaf records exactly five commands: focused pytest including real consumers, scoped Ruff check plus format-check, comment hygiene, owned-path diff integrity, and untimed worktree-venv `make verify`. All four remain open, unassigned, and unsigned.\n\nNo source/test file was edited. No leaf was claimed or transitioned; no plan review, completion verifier, test suite, implementation gate, commit, manual push, or close was run. The only mutations were normal rebar ticket events, auto-committed and auto-pushed by the MCP server.","timestamp":1788629507621137265},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Progress at origin/main@88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:\n- Confirmed the uv mismatch remains reproducible on main and added evidence to existing bug foliated-correct-arcticfox; no duplicate.\n- The four inherited async review jobs were stale-running. Restarted autositic-scarlet-clam, couped-parttime-nag, sphalerite-bereft-tortoise, and priceless-hotheaded-annelid against origin/main; no duplicate runs.\n- A claim attempt for certified leaf cordial-vulpine-piglet made no state change because parent written-peerless-kusimanse is unsigned. This confirms leaves must all be certified before story/epic certification and parent-first execution.\n- audit_subdivine_zebraic repaired four leaves: 72 paths, 185 allowlisted blocks, 20 DD commands, strict readback clean.\n- Root audited florid-gelatinous-doe: 38 blocks / 18 byte-stable paths; replaced its generic plan, exact impacts, and seven-command verification contract. It remains open/unassigned/unsigned pending independent audit and review.\n- MCP show/status calls continued to queue behind gates; local read-only CLI fallback confirmed the same stale attestations. Existing MCP bug skaldic-carbon-copperhead covers this behavior.","timestamp":1788629924823515605}],"created_at":1788584670051760001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2d